A||N||7||contra||Is there any way to temporarly fix my manifold crack??||||11||
Z||000000||contra||07-31-2000||06:05 PM||||I've got a small crack which is getting worse and i'm going to get it fixed up by next month, but for the time being is there any way to patch it up until then? I've tried this exhaust cement stuff, it works for about a day then it cracks and falls off. I've also tried exhaust tape (metallic stuff), and it melted a hole right through that. I'm wondering if anyone has any ingenius ideas for me.<BR>thanx<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||batboy||07-31-2000||08:02 PM||||Take the manifold off and have it welded. That's the only temporary fix I can think of. I say this is temporary, because usually if it cracked once, the metal is brittle and fatigued, thus will probably crack again in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||07-31-2000||08:34 PM||||gum<P><BR>this post is not seriously implying that you put gum on the manifold.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||contra||07-31-2000||08:52 PM||||heh gum<P>batboy: i have an extra manifold i'm just going to replace it, it's just going to be expensive because the mechanic has to take out a bunch of crap to get at some of the screws so i'm paying mostly in labor :/<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||nivlek68||07-31-2000||10:44 PM||||Magnum steel is what i used its held up for 2 months, no leak yet.||||reg||1
Z||000005||contra||07-31-2000||10:49 PM||||yeah?<BR>where would i be able to get that?<BR>and how is it applied? is it like a paste or is it a metal tape or something else?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||08-01-2000||12:20 PM||||j.b. weld?||||reg||1
Z||000007||nivlek68||08-01-2000||03:30 PM||||magnum steel is a industrial epoxy stick that begains to harden in 3-5 minutes. <BR>you cut off a piece and knead (mix) 30 seconds to a minute.then apply to surface to be repaired.i got mine at advance auto parts store.it can be ,drilled,sanded,tapped,machined,and painted after 1 hour. use on iron,aluminum,bronze,plastic,steel,cooper,wood,brass.  the package also says that they have 44221 magnum marine/plastic repair epoy stick. if ican find it, i was going to see if it would work on my riped panel.oh the part no.for mag. steel is 44020. good luck on your search, you might be able to find it at another parts store.   <BR>nivlek68||||reg||1
